            <ArticleTitle>Aberrant external jugular vein phlebectasia with tongue pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>148-50</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We have not encountered any other report of phlebectasia with tongue pain in the literature. The pain disappeared after the anomalous venous communication was excised.</AbstractText>
